    "narrative": "With a sparse schedule for the Austin Waves today, the offensive burden rests heavily on **Jackson Merrill**, who anchors our lineup with a 66.69 efficiency score. Despite facing an aggressive arm in May, **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a high-leverage spot in the #2 hole and a favorable platoon matchup that adds 13% to his base projection. While **Drake Baldwin** earns a spot at 49.93, his matchup against Yamamoto is difficult; his value is propped up solely by the leadoff volume. The remaining slots are essentially bridge plays, as **Kyle Tucker** (47.69) and **Andy Pages** (43.18) both face the elite craft of Sale. While **Kyle Tucker** remains an elite talent, the combination of a daunting SP_xERA and a suppressed order position makes this a volume-dependent day for the outfield.\n\nThe decision-making process was simplified by a slate void of our heavy hitters, as **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** are sidelined by team off-days. Among the reserves, no player reached the 40-point threshold required to displace our current starters, though **Heliot Ramos** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** were monitored closely for potential lineup shifts. With **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** officially confirmed on the IL, the depth chart is currently static. We are proceeding with caution, as the combination of Sale and Yamamoto creates significant downside risk for our scoring ceiling; we are essentially playing for high-contact, low-probability outcomes from **Drake Baldwin** and the rest of the bottom-third of the order.",
